{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{subtitle: Robert Burns (1788), traditional Scottish tune - public domain}
{key: C}
# Testo: https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Poetical_Works_of_Robert_Burns/Auld_Lang_Syne (ed. 1887)
# Accordi: https://de.wikibooks.org/wiki/Liederbuch/_Auld_Lang_Syne (CC BY-SA)
# Verso 4: l'edizione 1887 stampa "And days o' lang syne?"; qui la forma cantata,
# con "auld", come nella melodia della fonte degli accordi.
# Licenza di questo file: CC BY-SA 4.0 https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
# Modifiche rispetto alla fonte: convertito in ChordPro, righe divise per lo schermo
# del CardputerZero, note e sottotitoli in inglese; testo di pubblico dominio integrato dove serviva.
{comment: The first F of the chorus is only on the pickup "For"}

Should [C]auld acquaintance [G]be forgot,
and [C]never brought to [F]min'?
Should [C]auld acquaintance [G]be forgot,
and [C]days o' [Am]auld lang [C]syne?

{start_of_chorus}
[F]For [C]auld lang [G]syne, my dear,
[F]for [C]auld lang [F]syne,
we'll [C]tak a cup o' [G]kindness yet
for [C]auld [Am]lang [C]syne.
{end_of_chorus}

We [C]twa hae run a[G]bout the braes,
and [C]pu'd the gowans [F]fine,
but we've [C]wander'd mony a [G]weary foot
sin [C]auld [Am]lang [C]syne.

{chorus}

We [C]twa hae paidl't [G]i' the burn,
from [C]mornin sun till [F]dine;
but [C]seas between us [G]braid hae roar'd
sin [C]auld [Am]lang [C]syne.

{chorus}

And [C]here's a hand, my [G]trusty fiere,
and [C]gie's a hand o' [F]thine;
and we'll [C]tak a right guid [G]willie-waught,
for [C]auld [Am]lang [C]syne.

{chorus}

And [C]surely ye'll be your [G]pint-stowp,
and [C]surely I'll be [F]mine;
and we'll [C]tak a cup o' [G]kindness yet
for [C]auld [Am]lang [C]syne.

{chorus}
